{
  "_comment": "Verbatim copies of the files stage_on_pass_review reads for stage_phase1, from seven published benchmark-data cells — five for R1_CITED_CONSTANT_NOT_IN_ITS_SOURCE and R2_TOP_MODULE_PROVENANCE_REFUTED (#1845), two for R1_CITED_INPUT_ABSENT (#1854, folded in here because the doctrine forbids two PRs declaring one stage's block). Nothing here is authored and nothing is trimmed: each sha256 below is the source file's, and an input document is carried WHOLE, because a truncated input would let this fixture choose what the design input says — which is the one thing these rules must never do. The corpus-bound tests re-read the live cells for the whole-cell numbers; this fixture is what makes the controls run on a checkout that has no corpus.",
  "_why_one_input_is_gzipped": "`reject_pcie_gen5/.../pcie_gen5_spec.txt` ships gzipped, and that is a workaround for a false positive in another gate rather than anything about this rule. The published document quotes press-release URLs of the form `https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/<id>/en/...`, and `shipped_path_portability_check` R1 reads the `/home/<id>/` segment of a URL as a personal home path — measured, 5 findings, turning a gate that is PASS on main RED. Trimming those lines out was not an option: it would make the fixture choose what the input says. Fixing R1 to know a URL from a filesystem path is a change to a repo-wide blocking gate and belongs to that gate, not to this one. So the bytes are carried intact and unscanned. `decompressed_sha256` below is the PUBLISHED file's own hash and is asserted on every run, so the compression hides nothing: `gunzip -c` reproduces the cell byte for byte.",
  "corpus_repo": "https://github.com/vibeic/benchmark-data",
