  "_why_every_tree_carries_both_rules_inputs": "The stage carries TWO rules, and a tree holding only one rule's documents is not a run — it is one rule's slice of one. Measured before these were completed: composing the rules over trees that each answered one of them took the stage from 76 ACCEPT / 5 REJECT / 24 NOT CHECKED to 10 / 1 / 94, because a rule that could not look reported rc 2 over a rule that had proved a contradiction. The verdict precedence was fixed in the program; these trees were completed so the fixtures state a whole run either way. Every file added is verbatim from the SAME published cell the tree already named — no tree changed cell.",
  "_omitted": "`accept_lpddr5` drops one file the published cell carries, `input/docs/lpddr5_spec.pdf` (541 KB). Only text suffixes are read as design input, so that PDF is not an input this review can read on the live cell either — omitting it ships 541 KB no test opens and changes the file set the review sees by nothing."
}
